IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 6 (FREQUENCY PLANNING, ss 22 to 24) and PART 7 (BROADCASTING CONDITIONS, ss 25 to 28).
-- These rules state the 2024 consolidation. Section 23 is repealed (Act 22 of 2016): no rule.

§ `22. Frequency planning criteria`

-- src:1470 | 22. In performing its functions under this Act, the Authority must
-- src:1471 | have regard to —
-- src:1473 | (a) the social and economic characteristics within Singapore;
-- src:1475 | (b) the number of existing broadcasting services and the
-- src:1476 | demand for new broadcasting services;
-- src:1478 | (c) the developments in technology;
-- src:1480 | (d) the technical restraints relating to the transmission,
-- src:1481 | delivery or reception of broadcasting services;
-- src:1483 | (e) the demand for electromagnetic, and particularly radio
-- src:1484 | frequency, spectrum for services other than broadcasting
-- src:1485 | services; and
-- src:1487 | (f) any other matters that the Authority considers appropriate.
@ref s 22(a) to (f) (src:1470-1487)
-- What the Authority must have regard to in performing its functions under the Act: a matter on the list, or any other matter it considers appropriate.
GIVEN `it is the social and economic characteristics within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the number of existing broadcasting services and the demand for new broadcasting services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the developments in technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the technical restraints relating to the transmission, delivery or reception of broadcasting services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the demand for electromagnetic, and particularly radio frequency, spectrum for services other than broadcasting services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another matter the Authority considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22 the Authority must have regard to the matter` MEANS
    `it is the social and economic characteristics within Singapore` OR `it is the number of existing broadcasting services and the demand for new broadcasting services` OR `it is the developments in technology` OR `it is the technical restraints relating to the transmission, delivery or reception of broadcasting services` OR `it is the demand for electromagnetic, and particularly radio frequency, spectrum for services other than broadcasting services` OR `it is another matter the Authority considers appropriate`

§ `24. Separate licence for use of frequency not required`

-- src:1495 | 24. Despite anything in the Telecommunications Act 1999, if a
-- src:1496 | licensee is granted a broadcasting licence under this Act and the
-- src:1497 | licence includes the right for the licensee to use any specified
-- src:1498 | frequency in the electromagnetic spectrum or satellite orbits for the
-- src:1499 | broadcast, or the transmission of one or more broadcasting services,
-- src:1500 | then the licensee is not required to obtain any other licence under this
-- src:1501 | Act or the Telecommunications Act 1999 in respect of the use of such
-- src:1502 | frequency or satellite orbits for the period for which that broadcasting
-- src:1503 | licence is in force and for the purposes permitted by that licence.
@ref s 24 (src:1495-1503)
GIVEN `the licensee is granted a broadcasting licence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence includes the right to use a specified frequency in the electromagnetic spectrum or satellite orbits for the broadcast or transmission of one or more broadcasting services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is within the period for which that broadcasting licence is in force and for the purposes the licence permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24 the licensee must obtain another licence under this Act or the Telecommunications Act 1999 for the use of that frequency or those satellite orbits` MEANS
    IF `the licensee is granted a broadcasting licence under this Act` AND `the licence includes the right to use a specified frequency in the electromagnetic spectrum or satellite orbits for the broadcast or transmission of one or more broadcasting services` AND `the use is within the period for which that broadcasting licence is in force and for the purposes the licence permits`
    THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `25. Transmission area requirements`

-- src:1514 | 25.—(1) A broadcasting licensee must, within the time that may be
-- src:1515 | specified in its broadcasting licence, broadcast in a manner that
-- src:1516 | enables its broadcasting services to be received to the satisfaction of
-- src:1517 | the Authority in all parts of Singapore or any parts of Singapore that
-- src:1518 | the Authority may specify.
@ref s 25(1) (src:1514-1518)
GIVEN `the licensee broadcasts, within the time specified in its licence, in a manner that enables its services to be received to the Authority's satisfaction in all parts of Singapore or the parts the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) the broadcasting licensee has complied` MEANS
    `the licensee broadcasts, within the time specified in its licence, in a manner that enables its services to be received to the Authority's satisfaction in all parts of Singapore or the parts the Authority specifies`

-- src:1520 | (2) If the Authority so directs, a free-to-air licensee must publish, in
-- src:1521 | the manner that the Authority may require, notice of the
-- src:1522 | commencement dates for broadcasting its broadcasting services
-- src:1523 | and the areas of Singapore within which its broadcasting services
-- src:1524 | may be received satisfactorily.
@ref s 25(2) (src:1520-1524)
GIVEN `the Authority has directed it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has published, as the Authority requires, notice of the commencement dates and the areas of Singapore in which its services may be received satisfactorily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) the free-to-air licensee has complied` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has directed it` THEN JUST `the licensee has published, as the Authority requires, notice of the commencement dates and the areas of Singapore in which its services may be received satisfactorily` ELSE NOTHING

§ `26. Sharing of facilities`

-- src:1528 | 26.—(1) The Authority may direct any broadcasting licensee or
-- src:1529 | broadcasting apparatus licensee to coordinate and cooperate, in such
-- src:1530 | manner and on such terms as the Authority may specify, with any
-- src:1531 | other licensee or any other person specified by the Authority in the
-- src:1532 | use or sharing of any broadcasting apparatus or related equipment or
-- src:1533 | facility (other than a telecommunication system licensed under
-- src:1534 | section 5 of the Telecommunications Act 1999) owned, operated or
-- src:1535 | used by the broadcasting licensee or broadcasting apparatus licensee
-- src:1536 | for the purpose of broadcasting, whether or not they have been
-- src:1537 | provided, or are intended to be provided, by the licensee or any other
-- src:1538 | licensee or any other person specified by the Authority.
@ref s 26(1) (src:1528-1538)
GIVEN `the person is a broadcasting licensee or a broadcasting apparatus licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is a telecommunication system licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to coordinate and cooperate in the use or sharing of the broadcasting apparatus or related equipment or facility` MEANS
    `the person is a broadcasting licensee or a broadcasting apparatus licensee` AND (NOT `the facility is a telecommunication system licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act 1999`)

-- src:1540 | (2) The Authority may direct any broadcasting licensee to
-- src:1541 | coordinate and cooperate, in such manner and on such terms as the
-- src:1542 | Authority may specify, with any telecommunication licensee in the
-- src:1543 | use or sharing of any, or part of any, installation, plant or system
-- src:1544 | owned or used by the telecommunication licensee, where the
-- src:1545 | Authority is of the view that such coordination and cooperation is
-- src:1546 | necessary for the provision of any broadcasting service.
@ref s 26(2) (src:1540-1546)
GIVEN `the Authority is of the view that coordination and cooperation with the telecommunication licensee is necessary for the provision of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to coordinate and cooperate with the telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    `the Authority is of the view that coordination and cooperation with the telecommunication licensee is necessary for the provision of a broadcasting service`

-- src:1551 | (3) In this section, “telecommunication licensee” and
-- src:1552 | “telecommunication system” have the meanings given by section 2
-- src:1553 | of the Telecommunications Act 1999.
@ref s 26(3) (src:1551-1553)
-- Borrowed from section 2 of the Telecommunications Act 1999 (Encoder TA's side): the meaning is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `it is a telecommunication licensee or telecommunication system within the meaning of section 2 of the Telecommunications Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(3) the person or thing is a telecommunication licensee or telecommunication system` MEANS
    `it is a telecommunication licensee or telecommunication system within the meaning of section 2 of the Telecommunications Act 1999`

§ `27. Inspection and testing of broadcasting apparatus`

-- src:1557 | 27.—(1) The Authority or any person authorised by it in that behalf
-- src:1558 | may, at any reasonable time, inspect and test any broadcasting
-- src:1559 | apparatus used, or intended to be used, by a broadcasting apparatus
-- src:1560 | licensee for the transmission of any broadcasting service for the
-- src:1561 | purpose of ascertaining whether or not the licensee is complying, or
-- src:1562 | will comply, at all times with the broadcast standards prescribed by
-- src:1563 | this Act or the regulations, any Code of Practice and the conditions of
-- src:1564 | its broadcasting apparatus licence in respect of the transmission of
-- src:1565 | broadcasting services.
@ref s 27(1) (src:1557-1565)
GIVEN `the person is the Authority or a person it authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the apparatus is used, or intended to be used, by a broadcasting apparatus licensee for the transmission of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) the person may inspect and test the broadcasting apparatus` MEANS
    `the person is the Authority or a person it authorised` AND `the time is reasonable` AND `the apparatus is used, or intended to be used, by a broadcasting apparatus licensee for the transmission of a broadcasting service`

-- src:1567 | (2) For the purpose of any inspection or test under subsection (1),
-- src:1568 | the directors, principal officers and other employees of a broadcasting
-- src:1569 | apparatus licensee must —
-- src:1571 | (a) make available on request to the Authority or any person
-- src:1572 | authorised by the Authority for the purpose of the
-- src:1573 | inspection or test, and permit to be inspected and tested,
-- src:1574 | any part of its broadcasting apparatus used, or intended to
-- src:1575 | be used, for the transmission of any broadcasting service;
-- src:1577 | (b) assist the Authority or such authorised person in carrying
-- src:1578 | out the inspection or test in any manner specified by it; and
-- src:1580 | (c) answer directly and truthfully any question put to them by
-- src:1581 | the Authority or such authorised person.
@ref s 27(2)(a) to (c) (src:1567-1581)
GIVEN `the licensee's directors, principal officers and other employees made the apparatus available on request and permitted it to be inspected and tested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they assisted in carrying out the inspection or test in the manner specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they answered directly and truthfully any question put to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the directors, officers and employees have done what the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the licensee's directors, principal officers and other employees made the apparatus available on request and permitted it to be inspected and tested` AND `they assisted in carrying out the inspection or test in the manner specified` AND `they answered directly and truthfully any question put to them`

§ `28. Provision of building space, etc., by developer or owner of building or land`

-- src:1586 | 28.—(1) Where the Authority —
-- src:1588 | (a) considers it necessary that any licensable broadcasting
-- src:1589 | service should be provided to any building; and
-- src:1591 | (b) is of the opinion that any broadcasting apparatus or
-- src:1592 | installation or plant to be used in providing the service
-- src:1593 | has to be installed within the building or any land,
-- src:1598 | the Authority may by direction require the developer or owner of the
-- src:1599 | building or land to provide, within the period that may be specified in
-- src:1600 | the direction, such broadcasting apparatus, installation or plant or
-- src:1601 | space, of a standard acceptable to the Authority, within or on the
-- src:1602 | building or land and access thereto as the Authority may require.
@ref s 28(1) (src:1586-1602)
GIVEN `the Authority considers it necessary that a licensable broadcasting service should be provided to the building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is of the opinion that broadcasting apparatus or installation or plant to be used has to be installed within the building or any land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) the Authority may by direction require the developer or owner to provide the apparatus, installation or plant or space, and access` MEANS
    `the Authority considers it necessary that a licensable broadcasting service should be provided to the building` AND `the Authority is of the opinion that broadcasting apparatus or installation or plant to be used has to be installed within the building or any land`

-- src:1604 | (2) Where the Authority —
-- src:1606 | (a) considers it necessary that the reception of any licensable
-- src:1607 | broadcasting service in any building in any area should be
-- src:1608 | facilitated; and
-- src:1610 | (b) is of the opinion that any broadcasting apparatus or
-- src:1611 | installation or plant to be used in facilitating such
-- src:1612 | reception has to be installed within or on any building or
-- src:1613 | land in that area or any other area,
-- src:1615 | the Authority may by direction require the developer or owner of the
-- src:1616 | building or land to provide, within the period that may be specified in
-- src:1617 | the direction, access to the building or land and access to or
-- src:1618 | interconnection with any broadcasting apparatus or installation or
-- src:1619 | plant within or on the building or land.
@ref s 28(2) (src:1604-1619)
GIVEN `the Authority considers it necessary that reception of a licensable broadcasting service in the building in the area should be facilitated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is of the opinion that apparatus or installation or plant to be used has to be installed within or on a building or land in that area or any other area` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) the Authority may by direction require the developer or owner to provide access to the building or land and to or interconnection with the apparatus` MEANS
    `the Authority considers it necessary that reception of a licensable broadcasting service in the building in the area should be facilitated` AND `the Authority is of the opinion that apparatus or installation or plant to be used has to be installed within or on a building or land in that area or any other area`

-- src:1621 | (3) Any direction under subsection (1) or (2) may include —
-- src:1623 | (a) a requirement that the developer or owner of the building
-- src:1624 | or land must contribute wholly or partly to such costs and
-- src:1625 | expenses incurred for the provision of any broadcasting
-- src:1626 | apparatus, installation or plant or space under
-- src:1627 | subsection (1) as the Authority may determine; and
-- src:1629 | (b) any other requirements that the Authority may specify.
@ref s 28(3) (src:1621-1629)
GIVEN `it is a requirement that the developer or owner contribute wholly or partly to the costs and expenses of providing apparatus, installation or plant or space, as the Authority determines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is any other requirement the Authority may specify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3) a direction under subsection (1) or (2) may include this requirement` MEANS
    IF `it is a requirement that the developer or owner contribute wholly or partly to the costs and expenses of providing apparatus, installation or plant or space, as the Authority determines` OR `it is any other requirement the Authority may specify` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1631 | (4) Any person who fails to comply with any requirement in a
-- src:1632 | direction under subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:1633 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.
@ref s 28(4) (guilt) (src:1631-1633)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement in a direction under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person fails to comply with a requirement in a direction under subsection (1) or (2)`

-- src:1631 | (4) Any person who fails to comply with any requirement in a
-- src:1632 | direction under subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:1633 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.
@ref s 28(4) (punishment) (src:1631-1633)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 28(4) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 10000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is provided`
                  , `daily fine` IS `no further daily fine is provided`
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:1635 | (5) Nothing in any direction given under subsection (1) is to be
-- src:1636 | construed as granting any exemption from any licensing requirement
-- src:1637 | under this Act or any other written law which the developer or the
-- src:1638 | owner of any building or land may be required to comply with in
-- src:1639 | respect of any broadcasting apparatus or installation or plant.
@ref s 28(5) (src:1635-1639)
GIVEN `a direction under subsection (1) has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(5) the direction grants an exemption from a licensing requirement under this Act or any other written law` MEANS
    IF `a direction under subsection (1) has been given` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1644 | (6) In this section, “installation or plant” includes all buildings,
-- src:1645 | lands, structures, machinery, equipment, cables, poles and lines used
-- src:1646 | or intended for use in connection with broadcasting.
@ref s 28(6) "installation or plant" (src:1644-1646)
GIVEN `it is a building, land, structure, machinery, equipment, cable, pole or line used or intended for use in connection with broadcasting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(6) installation or plant includes this thing` MEANS
    IF `it is a building, land, structure, machinery, equipment, cable, pole or line used or intended for use in connection with broadcasting` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
